From: Marionette AirDrop driver research
Subject: [fuxi runtime] allocate the CPU-only PE session table virtually

During a captured ordinary-Wi-Fi startup, pe_open+0xb8 fails its session-table
allocation with order:5, GFP_KERNEL. There is free memory but no order-5 pages;
this occurs before monitor creation and does not diagnose firmware concurrency.
The PE session array is host-only, indexed through CPU virtual pointers and
not DMA mapped. Use the existing zeroing qdf_mem_valloc/vfree pair instead of
requiring physical contiguity. Change both failure and normal teardown paths.
No allocator retry loop, reclaim settings, DMA allocation or kernel checks
are changed. Pinned source audit found only these two table frees.

diff --git a/qcacld-3.0/core/mac/src/pe/lim/lim_api.c b/qcacld-3.0/core/mac/src/pe/lim/lim_api.c
--- a/qcacld-3.0/core/mac/src/pe/lim/lim_api.c
+++ b/qcacld-3.0/core/mac/src/pe/lim/lim_api.c
@@ -825,8 +825,10 @@
 		goto pe_open_timer_fail;
 	}
 
+	/* CPU-only session table: a large contiguous kmalloc can fail after
+	 * normal phone use fragments memory. No DMA mapping uses this table. */
 	mac->lim.gpSession =
-		qdf_mem_malloc(sizeof(struct pe_session) * mac->lim.maxBssId);
+		qdf_mem_valloc(sizeof(struct pe_session) * mac->lim.maxBssId);
 	if (!mac->lim.gpSession) {
 		status = QDF_STATUS_E_NOMEM;
 		goto pe_open_psession_fail;
@@ -865,7 +867,7 @@
 	return status; /* status here will be QDF_STATUS_SUCCESS */
 
 pe_open_lock_fail:
-	qdf_mem_free(mac->lim.gpSession);
+	qdf_mem_vfree(mac->lim.gpSession);
 	mac->lim.gpSession = NULL;
 pe_open_psession_fail:
 	qdf_mem_free(mac->lim.lim_timers.gpLimCnfWaitTimer);
@@ -907,7 +909,7 @@
 	qdf_mem_free(mac->lim.lim_timers.gpLimCnfWaitTimer);
 	mac->lim.lim_timers.gpLimCnfWaitTimer = NULL;
 
-	qdf_mem_free(mac->lim.gpSession);
+	qdf_mem_vfree(mac->lim.gpSession);
 	mac->lim.gpSession = NULL;
 
 	pe_free_dph_node_array_buffer();
